["er.eventlog.import-anchor/1",{"authority":{"logical_scope":"aep","stream_identity":"01a0d3bf-067c-7068-af65-bd964ce78fcb","tenant":"planning"},"completeness":"available_evidence_only","evidence":[],"instance":{"entity":"story","fields":{"body":"# Story: A native flow is governed by the engine at every section boundary\n\n## Outcome\n\n`b10x-harness workflow run` walks a flow that `protocol workflow flow` projected from `adp/default`,\nand that projection is an ordering, not a government: no guard travels. The loop asks a `transition`\nhook before a section is entered and after it leaves. `protocol drive transition` answers it from\nthe engine — `evaluate` for `enter`, `transition` on a copy of the execution for `leave` — so a\nnative walk is governed by the same documents that govern a driven run, with no crate dependency in\neither direction. Harness design 0003 § 7 named this E2; atlas ADR 0004 records the boundary.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Reads the loop's `transition` document on stdin; exit `0` proceeds, `2` refuses with\n  `{\"reason\": …}` in the engine's words; anything unreadable exits `1`, which the loop reads fail\n  closed.\n- `--run <id>` positions the engine on that run's snapshot over the store as it is now; without it,\n  on the state the flow path names (a step node after its state; a retreat group\n  `<first>-to-<last>` at its first state on `enter`, its last on `leave`).\n- A section that came out failed is left alone.\n- Decides only: writes nothing, takes no lock; a consultation leaves a run's cursor byte-identical.\n- Documented on the website (integrate-a-harness, CLI reference) and in `docs/guide/harness.md`.\n\n## Evidence\n\n`crates/protocol-cli/tests/drive_cli.rs`: nine `transition_*` tests over the real binary and a\nfixture store; the full gate.\n","document":{"events":[],"fields":{"$aep":{"archived":false,"metadata":{"created_at":0,"id":"ent-343e6523eba776e8e6941bb4e6dc0371","locator":"ep://planning/store/story/drive-transition-verb","provenance":{"created_by":"system","updated_by":"system"},"revision":5,"type":"aep.story/v1","updated_at":0}},"body":"# Story: A native flow is governed by the engine at every section boundary\n\n## Outcome\n\n`b10x-harness workflow run` walks a flow that `protocol workflow flow` projected from `adp/default`,\nand that projection is an ordering, not a government: no guard travels. The loop asks a `transition`\nhook before a section is entered and after it leaves. `protocol drive transition` answers it from\nthe engine — `evaluate` for `enter`, `transition` on a copy of the execution for `leave` — so a\nnative walk is governed by the same documents that govern a driven run, with no crate dependency in\neither direction. Harness design 0003 § 7 named this E2; atlas ADR 0004 records the boundary.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Reads the loop's `transition` document on stdin; exit `0` proceeds, `2` refuses with\n  `{\"reason\": …}` in the engine's words; anything unreadable exits `1`, which the loop reads fail\n  closed.\n- `--run <id>` positions the engine on that run's snapshot over the store as it is now; without it,\n  on the state the flow path names (a step node after its state; a retreat group\n  `<first>-to-<last>` at its first state on `enter`, its last on `leave`).\n- A section that came out failed is left alone.\n- Decides only: writes nothing, takes no lock; a consultation leaves a run's cursor byte-identical.\n- Documented on the website (integrate-a-harness, CLI reference) and in `docs/guide/harness.md`.\n\n## Evidence\n\n`crates/protocol-cli/tests/drive_cli.rs`: nine `transition_*` tests over the real binary and a\nfixture store; the full gate.\n","owner":"driver","relations":[{"decomposes":"epic:cross-harness-portability"},{"serves":"vision:O3"}],"status":"implemented","summary":"protocol drive transition answers the loop transition hook from evaluate and transition, so b10x-harness workflow run is governed without walking here","tags":["driver","harness"],"title":"A native flow is governed by the engine at every section boundary"},"lifecycle_state":"implemented"},"owner":"driver","relations":[{"decomposes":"epic:cross-harness-portability"},{"serves":"vision:O3"}],"summary":"protocol drive transition answers the loop transition hook from evaluate and transition, so b10x-harness workflow run is governed without walking here","tags":["driver","harness"],"title":"A native flow is governed by the engine at every section boundary"},"id":"ent-343e6523eba776e8e6941bb4e6dc0371","lifecycle_state":"implemented","revision":5,"version":1},"order":"per_kind_only","subject":["story","ent-343e6523eba776e8e6941bb4e6dc0371"]}]